{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.BraidedClosure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.BraidedClosure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.MarkovClosure","lean:module:QOU.OrientedSkein.SkeinDatum"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.braided_closure_eq_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.braided_closure_eq_markov","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L255-L267","doc":"**The closure of a braid in a braided category is the Markov trace.**  If the braiding on `E`\nis a Hecke crossing, the loop `d` is invertible and the curl is `w`, then the normalised closure\nof all strands agrees with every Markov trace family of parameter `z = w d⁻¹` on the Hecke tower\n(for instance the Ocneanu trace). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.braidedLeftTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.braidedLeftTrace","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L246-L253","doc":"**The exact-pairing instance**: close a strand by `η_{F,E}`, the braiding `β_{F,E}`, and\n`ε_{F,E}`; the loop value is the braided quantum dimension `qDimWith F E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.HeckeCrossing.ofBraiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.HeckeCrossing.ofBraiding","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L241-L244","doc":"The Hecke crossing given by the braiding, when it satisfies the Hecke quadratic relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closureLeftTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closureLeftTrace","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L219-L239","doc":"**An arbitrary cup and cap give a left trace** for the braiding crossing, given the loop value\n`u ≫ c = d • 𝟙` and the curl value `closeLeft (β_{E,E}) = w • 𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_leftCross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_leftCross","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L212-L217","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_id","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L203-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft_apply","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L200-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closeLeft","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L191-L198","doc":"Closing the leftmost strand with a cup `u` and a cap `c`, as an `R`-linear map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.closure2_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.closure2_conj","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L172-L180","doc":"The double closure with arbitrary cup and cap is invariant under moving the crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.leftCross_comm_whisker'_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.leftCross_comm_whisker'_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.leftCross_comm_whisker'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.leftCross_comm_whisker'","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L164-L170","doc":"A crossing of the two left strands commutes with anything on the strands to their right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_cross_nested","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_cross_nested","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L148-L162","doc":"**A crossing slides through a nested pair of caps**, from the right legs to the left legs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_cross_nested","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_cross_nested","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L132-L146","doc":"**A crossing slides through a nested pair of cups**, from the right legs to the left legs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.capOn_naturality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.capOn_naturality","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L126-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn_naturality_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn_naturality_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L119-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn_naturality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn_naturality","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L119-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.capOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.capOn","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L115-L117","doc":"A cap on the left of `Y`: `F ⊗ (E ⊗ Y) ⟶ Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cupOn","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L111-L113","doc":"A cup on the left of `Y`: `Y ⟶ F ⊗ (E ⊗ Y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_slide_left_leg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_slide_left_leg","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L100-L109","doc":"A strand crossing into a cap from the right exits across its left leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_slide_right_leg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cap_slide_right_leg","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L90-L98","doc":"A crossing entering the right leg of a cap moves to a crossing past its left leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_slide_left_leg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_slide_left_leg","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L79-L88","doc":"A strand crossing the left leg of a cup from the right moves to its other side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_slide_right_leg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OrientedSkein.cup_slide_right_leg","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OrientedSkein/BraidedClosure.lean#L69-L77","doc":"A crossing of the right leg of a cup with a strand on its right moves to the left leg. ","signatureChunk":0}]}